  35:     """
  36:     Move colored sprites from the left strip into a framed area at marker-defined targets.
  37: 
  38:     Input structure:
  39:     - bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.
  40: 
  41:     Rule:
  42:     - For each color, target rows/cols are where both opposite frame edges share that color. Targets are the Cartesian product.
  43:     - Erase each sprite from the left and stamp it centered at every target. Higher sprites cover lower ones.
  44: 
  45:     Key insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.
  46:     """
